* Designed a baseline anomaly detection mechanism using normal operational data
*Integrated Generative AI techniques to synthesize realistic cyber-attack scenarios
*Injected generated attacks into the Digital Twin instead of the real system
*Monitored system responses, safety violations, and anomaly scores during simulations
Identified hidden vulnerabilities such as single points of failure, blind spots, and unsafe states
* Exposed results through FastAPI endpoints and real-time WebSocket streams
*Visualized vulnerability concentration and system impact using interactive dashboards
* Validated that GenAI-generated attacks revealed weaknesses not detected by traditional approaches



6. Any challenges faced during Solution Development (250 words max)

A. One major challenge was adapting industrial control system behavior into a simplified yet realistic Digital Twin while maintaining meaningful security insights.
Another difficulty was integrating Generative AI outputs with structured system states in a controlled and interpretable manner. Running real-time APIs and simulations
within a Jupyter-based prototyping environment required careful handling of asynchronous execution and event loops. Additionally, ensuring that generated attack scenarios were realistic and relevant to industrial processes, rather than random anomalies, required iterative tuning and domain understanding. Despite these challenges, consolidating the solution into a unified orchestration pipeline enabled faster debugging, experimentation, and demonstration.


